For the completed robotic system, two main areas of validation were identified. Firstly, the ability of the robot to successfully navigate in a crowd and, secondly, correct feedback being timely provided to the user. A series of controlled experiments planned in Dalby Court, Imperial College London would be conducted with three different blindfolded participants, with informed consent. Multiple spotters will walk alongside the participant, one holding the emergency stop to ensure safety. The blindfolded participants are not fully representative of visually impaired users, which is an acknowledged limitation of this validation methodology. 


Each trial is a fix route of 50 m with varying conditions detailed below. Each run is conducted twice to ensure repeatability: 
