\end{figure}

RTAB-Map uses the 3D LiDAR point cloud for SLAM and generates a 2D occupancy grid for global navigation. The height threshold was chosen to avoid unnecessarily blocking paths with features the robot can traverse; such filtering alone does not establish terrain traversability. Figure~\ref{fig:indoor_navigation} shows the simulated environment and navigation visualisation in RViz.

